title: IainSchweblin0
---
Iain Schweblin: Iain slowly rises from the floor. He wipes his eyes and looks around the room. As his mental fog clears, he grabs his head and backs against the wall. He begins to hyperventilate. “Oh, God, Oh, God!”
-> Create a strange noise that comes from down the hall.
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    The sudden noise demands Iain’s focus. He takes a deep breath and continues down the hallway, hand sliding along the wall.
-> Drop the temperature.
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    The sudden blast of cold air demands Iain’s focus. He takes a deep breath and continues down the hallway, hand sliding along the wall.
-> Raise the lights.
    <<reduce_fear "Iain Schweblin">>
    <<determined "Iain Schweblin">>
    The bright light demands Iain’s focus. He takes a deep breath and continues down the hallway, hand sliding along the wall.
-> Do nothing. Let his mind spin.
    <<add_fear "Iain Schweblin">>
    <<discover_fear "Iain Schweblin" 0>>
    <<scared "Iain Schweblin">>
    //Overthinking
    Gasping for air, he tries to stand but comes crashing back to the floor. When his breathing finally slows, he forces himself back up and moves down the hall.  
===
title: IainSchweblin1
---
Iain Schweblin: Iain was used to the windswept peace of The Great Plains, but this place was different. There was a silent stillness so absolute that he could hear the sound of his pounding heart and the rhythmic whoosh of blood in his ears. 
->Let him settle into the silence.
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    The sound of his heart beating reminds him he's alive and in control.
->Create a dull sound from far off in the distance.
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    He looks around but finds nothing. 
->Fill his head with the sounds of people talking all around him.
    <<add_fear "Iain Schweblin">>
    <<discover_fear "Iain Schweblin" 1>>
    <<terrified "Iain Schweblin">>
    //Fear of crowds
    Iain grabs his head as the chatter of an imagined crowd grows louder and closer. When the voices slowly dissipate, he releases his breath but fears that he’s on the edge of panic.
->Create a sharp ringing noise.
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    Iain grabs his head. "Where the hell is that coming from?" He scrabbles further down the hall toward the assaulting alarm. 
===
title: IainSchweblin2
---
Iain Schweblin: As the minutes turn to hours, his mind goes back to Grace’s final place of rest. Did someone do this to him because of her? Who would stalk a dead wife's gravesite? Who would trap him in this agony?
->This place must be under the cemetery, like some lost catacombs.
    <<reduce_fear "Iain Schweblin">>
    <<determined "Iain Schweblin">>
    "That could be it!" The plausible explanation triggers a wave of hope.  
->Why would someone change the words on her gravestone?
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    No use speculating. He must keep moving.
->Her soul has trapped you here. You've been a neglectful father, careless with her children.
    <<add_fear "Iain Schweblin">>
    <<discover_fear "Iain Schweblin" 2>>    
    <<terrified "Iain Schweblin">>
    //Trauma from wife's death
    “I’m so sorry, Grace.” Tears stream down his cheeks and soak into his collar.
->You didn’t appreciate her enough while she was alive. This is God punishing you.
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    He pushes back against the allegation. He remembers the way she smiled when he walked in the door and the way she gasped at the sight of the flowers he’d brought with him.
===
title: IainSchweblin3
---
Iain Schweblin: Iain analyzes what happened before he blacked out, desperate for answers. 
->"There was a storm coming. Maybe a lightning strike? This could be a coma."
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    But Iain doesn't remember rain, so he casts the thought aside. 
->"The kids are still in the car."
    <<add_fear "Iain Schweblin">>
    <<discover_fear "Iain Schweblin" 3>>
    <<terrified "Iain Schweblin">>
    //Fear of harm coming to his kids
    “Oh, my God, THE KIDS!” He falls into a frenzy. "What happened to the kids? Are they in here, too? How will I get them back home?" Sweating through his shirt, he paces back and forth.
->"Someone else must have known you were coming to see Grace. You’ve been captured."
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    "Why would I be taken hostage??" He shakes the thought from his mind. 
->"Maybe you fell on the walk back to the car and hit your head."
    <<neutral "Iain Schweblin">>
    "There was no pain. That can’t be it." He shakes the thought from his mind. 
